{
  "apiVersion": 1,
  "type": "docs.detail.section",
  "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
  "data": {
    "id": "tailwind",
    "title": "Tailwind",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "bash",
        "code": "npm install @astryxdesign/core @stylexjs/stylex @astryxdesign/theme-neutral",
        "label": "Install"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "css",
        "code": "@layer reset, theme, base, astryx-base, astryx-theme, components, utilities;\n\n@import \"tailwindcss/theme.css\" layer(theme);\n@import \"tailwindcss/preflight.css\" layer(base);\n@import \"@astryxdesign/core/reset.css\";\n@import \"@astryxdesign/core/astryx.css\";\n@import \"@astryxdesign/theme-neutral/theme.css\";\n@import \"@astryxdesign/core/tailwind-theme.css\";\n@import \"tailwindcss/utilities.css\" layer(utilities);",
        "label": "globals.css"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "The `@layer` declaration is critical — without it, component styles outrank Tailwind utilities and `className` overrides stop working. The bridge (`tailwind-theme.css`) maps classes like `text-primary`, `bg-surface`, and `rounded-lg` to design tokens with no JS."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "A project with Tailwind already set up needs a smaller change, which `astryx docs styling-libraries/tailwind` shows. For Tailwind v3, see the layer workaround in `astryx docs migration/migration-setup`."
      }
    ],
    "links": {
      "up": "astryx docs styling-overview --index",
      "previous": "astryx docs styling-overview plain",
      "next": "astryx docs styling-overview stylex-own-code"
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "answeredBy": {
